From a455e4f681062e2c5c9c2ca674f8658fd89c93b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:31:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 40/40] dos: 16bpp blowup path without a library call per pixel

blowupOntoScreenNative() (patch 0018) packed every source pixel through
SDL_MapSurfaceRGB() -- a function call that re-derives the format each
time -- and spread it across its inBlowFactor-wide box with a two-byte
memcpy() per destination pixel: 1600 calls and 4800 tiny memcpys per
frame for a 100x16 image. Measured on the 486DX2-50 + Mach64 rig (patch
0037's STAGEDBG.LOG): 11.9 ms per frame, constant to 0.05 ms across
every window, for a 300x48 output. That is the second-largest fixed cost
in the frame after the world render, and far more than the pixel count
justifies.

For a 2-bytes-per-pixel, non-indexed, non-10-bit surface this reads the
per-channel bit counts and shifts once from the surface's
SDL_PixelFormatDetails and packs inline with the same arithmetic
SDL_MapRGB uses for that case -- (c >> (8 - bits)) << shift per channel,
OR'd with Amask (SDL_pixels.c) -- writing Uint16s straight into the row
buffer, then memcpys the row inBlowFactor times as before. Output is
identical by construction. The generic path is untouched and still
serves 24bpp and 32bpp.

Verified: DOSBox-X title-screen captures (320x240 16bpp, the same path
the rig negotiates) from the build before this patch and the build with
it differ in zero pixels (ImageMagick compare, AE metric, on a rendered
title with 13 distinct colors), and three full DOSBox-X lives on the
patched build ran clean (14.97-15.02 fps, fps_p95 14.98-14.99).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017TKEXpxndNddTzMQkSdtBX
